# Postgres safety

Wrap multi-statement schema changes in transactions when the migration tool
supports them.

Use `IF EXISTS` / `IF NOT EXISTS` on drops and creates when the surrounding
migrations already do. Do not drop tables or columns without a rollback note.

Do not grant superuser or `CREATEDB` to application roles. Match existing
role and search_path conventions.

Prefer explicit column lists over `SELECT *` in new application queries.
